#: package/analyses/bibliography.description
msgid ""
"A curated, verified bibliography of the methodological sources cited "
"throughout AssumptionsLab, not a data analysis: it renders a topic-filtered "
"reading list in APA 7th edition and does not read or compute anything from "
"the user's dataset. References can be filtered by topic (statistical "
"assumptions, normality, homoscedasticity, linearity and regression, path "
"analysis, related groups, time series, robust methods) and displayed in "
"English or Spanish, with citation style always fixed to APA 7th. Use it to "
"trace a diagnostic back to its source literature or to build a reference "
"list for a methods section."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/assumptionLibrary.description
msgid ""
"A methodological reference glossary, not a data analysis: it explains what "
"each statistical assumption and test covered by AssumptionsLab means, why it "
"matters, and when it applies, without computing anything from the user's "
"dataset. Entries can be filtered by category (e.g. normality, "
"homoscedasticity, linearity, independence, multicollinearity, "
"outliers/influence, sphericity, proportional odds, robust alternatives) and "
"are available in English or Spanish. Use it alongside any of the "
"assumption-checking analyses to look up the theory behind a diagnostic, or "
"as a stand-alone teaching aid for planning an analysis before running one."
msgstr ""

